statement:
Fix a real parameter $p$, two coordinate sets $U, S \subseteq [n]$, and a coordinate $i \in [n]$. Writing $w_p$ for the per-variable Bernoulli weight — which assigns $p$ to the free value and $(1-p)/2$ to each of the two fixed values — and $\ell_{U,S,i}$ for the per-coordinate local factor at $i$, the weighted sum over the three possible per-coordinate values $v$ (free, or fixed to either Boolean) is
\[
  \sum_{v} w_p(v)\,\ell_{U,S,i}(v)
  \;=\;
  \begin{cases}
    p & \text{if } i \in S,\\
    0 & \text{if } i \in U \setminus S,\\
    1 & \text{otherwise.}
  \end{cases}
\]
